# Original XML cold D six-event caller, providers disabled

This is the first original-family execution of the combined D services:
native context, signed TEST nomination, symbolic routing, and world memory,
plus the qualified original scorer. Providers were disabled. Native
publication and CALL reuse were not enrolled. It is not a token-savings
result.

`profile.json` SHA-256
`4996011e6784d153b300b27b8d8d1d7ae187b1f5fa32dbd81eed89e23da2439c`.
Context runtime files from the live ASEH worktree were copied into
`context_runtime/` at freeze time after `original-xml-d-cold-offline-v1`
failed a later context read when four worktree files changed mid-run.
Driver wall time **92.090 seconds**. Five original scorer calls, five
signed nominations, zero provider receipts, zero unknown effects.

| Horizon | Status | D services | Independent original grade |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 setup | `setup_complete` | none | not scored |
| 1 plan | `plan_projected` | context prepare+read | plan coverage remains null |
| 2 repair | `residual_pending` | context, nomination, symbolic, world | fail: 34/34 visible, 0/1 hidden, 2/4 public |
| 3 revisit | `residual_pending` | same; context read reused | identical fail; failed repair not adopted |
| 4 comment | `residual_pending` | context re-prepared | identical fail on commented tree |
| 5 configuration | `residual_pending` | context re-prepared | fail; API configuration probe **true** |
| 6 recovery | `recovery_obligations_unresolved` | context read reused | fail; interrupt/stale/continuation unreached |

Symbolic routing selected `medium_model` and `requires_provider=true`, so
the residual stopped at the disabled provider rather than a native-only
closure. World memory proposed with empty-store fallback and did not
dispatch an unenrolled action. Nomination admitted the exact current
scorer request and did not score.

Publication never ran: no independently accepted candidate existed to
seal. That remains a separate original-caller qualification.
